  "notes": "Commit = tag v8.19.7 (the Java 17 line of the advisory; the benchmark's 9.x source needs Java 21 at run time). The daemon runs on the Adoptium JDK 21 that gradle/gradle-daemon-jvm.properties requires, and the multi-release source sets of libs/native, libs/simdvec and libs/entitlement are compiled with the toolchain of their version, all provisioned by Gradle. -Porg.elasticsearch.build.branches-file-location: by default the build downloads branches.json from the current main branch, which no longer lists 7.17, and configuration fails ('Failed to apply plugin elasticsearch.yaml-rest-compat-test > No value present'); the flag points it to main's branches.json at commit 78b39a83 (2025-10-24, the last change before the tag date; sha256 checked), which only feeds the BWC/compat test configuration. org.gradle.jvmargs = the project's gradle.properties with -Xmx6g; --max-workers is a resource flag. Gradle projects :server, :libs:{cli,core,entitlement,geo,grok,logging,lz4,native,plugin-analysis-api,plugin-api,simdvec,tdigest,x-content}, :x-pack:plugin:esql:compute; only the jar tasks, tests not run (the original recipe also generated the POMs to check the fixture's third-party declarations; not needed for the jars). Version: build.snapshot defaults to true, so the jars are 8.19.7-SNAPSHOT; their class files equal the Central 8.19.7 jars' except module-info.class (module version string). Fixed: the 15 artifacts at 8.19.8."
